\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces (a) Schematic diagram of the Michelson interferometer setup. A source of light enters a beam splitter which then directs two beams into a fixed and a movable mirror. The two separate beams then are reflected back into the splitter where they recombine and enter the detector. (b) A graph displaying the intensity of the interferometry pattern based on the path difference, or the difference in distances between the two mirrors. Source: Peter Reece PHYS3114 Lectures}}{2}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:interferometer}{{3}{2}{(a) Schematic diagram of the Michelson interferometer setup. A source of light enters a beam splitter which then directs two beams into a fixed and a movable mirror. The two separate beams then are reflected back into the splitter where they recombine and enter the detector. (b) A graph displaying the intensity of the interferometry pattern based on the path difference, or the difference in distances between the two mirrors. Source: Peter Reece PHYS3114 Lectures}{figure.caption.11}{}}
